Title: Solving the Measurement Problem: A Comprehensive Model Based on Three
  Postulates
Authors: Ajax Benander
Categories: quant-ph
Comments: 10 pages
License: http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/
\\
  The measurement problem is one of the most notorious and difficult open
questions in all of physics. Why is it that quantum states seem to change their
appearance just because of viewing or lack thereof? In the following paper, a
possible solution will be explained using only three simple postulates which
seek to generalize the concept of quantum superposition beyond just the
subatomic world, and in the process remove any hints of questionable
anthropocentric bias from the quantum theory. At its finest, this reasoning is
potentially at once the missing piece to quantum theory that Einstein longed
for, and the confirmation of correctness that Bohr was after.
\\

