arXiv:submit/4912036
From: Ajax Benander <akb9408@rit.edu>
Date: Tue, 23 May 2023 13:59:35 EST   (41kb)

Title: Why Terrestrial Natural History is the Optimal Path to Generate Human
  Life
Authors: Ajax Benander
Categories: q-bio.OT astro-ph.EP stat.AP
Comments: 28 pages
License: http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/
\\
  Serving as a followup to the previous paper regarding the existential
importance of dinosaurs and the formulation of the accordance principle, in
this paper a whole list of results pertaining to various applications of the
accordance principle will be presented. Such results range from the importance
of the mass of the impactor Chicxulub to the origin of primates, and beyond.
Generally, this paper concerns the art of using the very state of our Bayesian
perspective in the universe to predict and derive aspects and effects of the
Earth's past and present which would have been otherwise inaccessible. It
should be noted that these products are but the very beginning of what is
possible with this new logical system, and if anything they are meant to serve
as a guide both for what is and can be known on this topic, altogether working
as a process of converting just the right known information on our past and
present into further information which would otherwise be near impossible to
gather by other means.
\\

