Dear Mr. Benander,

I have read your manuscript, A Condensed Overview of the Aethic Solution to the Measurement Problem, submitted to Synthese

Before it can be sent out for review, I would request that you carry out the corrections below.
You are kindly requested to also check the website for possible attachment(s).


While submitting, please check the filled in author data carefully and update them if applicable - they need to be complete and correct in order for the revision to be processed further.

Please submit your revised manuscript by accessing the following site:

https://www.editorialmanager.com/synt/

Your username is: AjaxB 
If you forgot your password, you can click the 'Send Login Details' link on the EM Login page.

We are looking forward to receiving your revised manuscript before 04 May 2025

Please note: When uploading your revised manuscript files, please make sure only to submit your editable source files (i.e. Word, Tex). PDF is not allowed at this stage.

With kind regards,
Wiebe van der Hoek
Editor in Chief
Synthese

Comments to the author (if any):
Dear Ajax,

thanks for your Synthese submission. I have two strong suggestions before sending this out for review. First of all, I know from experience that it is close to impossible to find reviewers for a manuscript over 30 pages. I suggest you make your arguments in a more succinct way. Secondly, there is very little engagement with the contemporary literature on the subject: only two relevant papers from this century are referenced. Is this actually a discussion that is still relevant for the Philosophy of Science?

Best wishes, Wiebe van der Hoek
Editor-in-Chief





