Dear Mr. Benander,

I have received the decision from the Editor on your manuscript, SYNT-D-25-00828R1 "Extrusion Without Duplication: Aethic Time, Collapse, and Observer-Relative Reality"

With regret, I must inform you that the Editors have decided that your manuscript cannot be accepted for publication in Synthese.

This is an editorial decision, as the work was not sent out for review. Please scroll down all the way to the end of this message for a brief justification of this decision.
You are kindly requested to also check the website for possible reviewer attachment(s).


I would like to thank you very much for forwarding your manuscript to us for consideration and wish you every success in finding an alternative place of publication.

With kind regards,
Springer Journals Editorial Office
Synthese

The Editorial Manager is at:
https://www.editorialmanager.com/synt/


Dear Ajax,

thanks for your Synthese submission. Unfortunately, I have now decided not to continue sending it out for review. I have contacted 17 potential reviewers, and several of them have come back saying that the paper is confused and immature. I suggest you share your work with some peers first, before trying a major journal. 

Best wishes with this project,

Wiebe van der Hoek
Editor-in-Chief


---

Message from Springer Nature, publisher of Synthese:


While we are sorry we cannot publish your work in Synthese,

our colleagues at the Springer Nature Transfer Desk would be delighted to help you find the right journal for your submission. This is a free service that provides authors with a range of journal suggestions tailored for each article. Please watch out for an email from the Transfer Desk with more information within the next 48 hours.

